kind how-do-i
title How do I let programs resize the console's grid, so that vtium-config can try a size?
intro vtium-config tries a size on the console by asking the console for the grid that size gives. The console does that only while allow-window-ops is on. vtium reads allow-window-ops when it starts, so a console that started with it off keeps it off until vtium starts again, even after you install a draft that turns it on.
see looks/try-a-whole-look-on-the-console

# The console started with allow-window-ops off.
file etc/vtium.conf
    version = 1
    font-name = mono
    [look plain]
    palette = legacy
    [head console]
    vt = 5
    look = plain
file etc/batch.conf
    ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf
font fonts/mono.bdf 8x16
frit mono
    source=bdf:ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf

1. Go to the Looks tab.
2. Press w to resize grid.
note vtium-config asks whether to let programs resize the grid.
3. Press y for yes.
4. Press i to install.
5. Press y for yes.
at the install
check installed has "allow-window-ops"

6. Choose plain.
7. Choose Size.
8. Choose 24 pt.
note The console still runs with allow-window-ops off, so vtium-config tries nothing and says when the size takes effect.
at the size
check console grid 100x30
check console never-received "\e[8;"
check screen shows "does not let programs resize its grid until vtium starts again"
9. Press Esc.
10. Press q to quit.

11. Restart vtium.
at the restart
check console font mono
